<title>POLAND: All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 362 million zlotys ($118.9 million) against a one billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold a total 298 million zlotys worth of the bills. ($ = 3.045 Polish Zlotys)  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price     --     95.08    90.55     --	82.60</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.20)  (90.79)    --     (82.90)</p>
<p>   new max price     --     95.32    90.85     --	83.20</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.28)  (90.88)    --     (83.40)</p>
<p>   offer		 --     300.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded     --	73.2     31.5     --	257.3</p>
<p>   bids accepted     --	63.2     31.5     --	203.3</p>
<p>   next auction     400.0   200.0    200.0     --	400.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
